# BuildKit applies this when building with -f clients/apps/web/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs repo-root-relative paths (clients/apps/web/...,
# clients/packages/ui, clients/packages/relationship-contract, and clients/packages/eslint-plugin-web),
# so the build context must be the repo root. This keeps that context to the
# four trees it reads — mirroring server/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
*
!clients/apps/web
!clients/packages/eslint-plugin-web
!clients/packages/relationship-contract
!clients/packages/ui

# Re-excluded after the allowlist above, so a working tree that has already been
# built or installed does not ship its output into the image context.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env*
